  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "cadences-applied",
      "title": "Cadences — Applied",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** theory | **Tier:** applied | **Difficulty:** 5/10\n**Prerequisites:** Cadences — Introduction\n**Tags:** cadences, phrase, deceptive"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Spot cadences in scores and tunes; connect them to **phrase structure** and bass lines."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "phrase-rhythm",
      "title": "Phrase rhythm",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Antecedent phrase often ends half cadence; consequent ends perfect. AABB tune forms map naturally to question–answer pairs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "inversions-at-cadence",
      "title": "Inversions at cadence",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "I6–V or cadential 6/4 embellishes dominant before resolution — common in classical; simplified in folk."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
