  "quiz_markdown": "### Q1. Antecedent often ends on V.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q2. Consequent often ends on I.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q3. Phrase pairs form period structure.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q4. Deceptive cadence delays tonic arrival.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q5. Cadential 6/4 precedes dominant.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q6. Applied cadences appear in tune analysis.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q7. Bass line defines cadence type.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q8. IV–I is plagal.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q9. Session tunes use clear cadence points for repeats.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q10. Half cadence invites another phrase.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q11. Voice-leading smooths V–I motion.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q12. Applied tier links to phrase-structure lesson.\n\n**Answer:** True",
